description:
Back-project a pixel (row, col) to a world XYZ point using the selected camera's precomputed world map. Row 0 = top of image, col 0 = left. Returns world_xyz in meters.

USE THIS to find where an object is in the world — look at the embedded high-resolution image returned by view_env_state to pick a pixel on the target object, then call back_project. The default resolution is high (1024x1024). Pass resolution='low' only for pixels from the embedded/standard 256 image. The pixel coordinates must come from the same camera and resolution requested here. Use camera='agentview' for global tabletop layout and object locations; use camera='wrist' for close-range details near the gripper, occlusions, and container/cabinet interiors. Sample several pixels on the object and median their xy for robustness.

REGION MODE: pass row_range=[r0,r1] and col_range=[c0,c1] instead of row/col to get the midpoint of world xy over that pixel window, with an optional world-z band (z_min, z_max). Use it for the center of a container cavity or flat region, where a single-pixel or mask-median estimate is biased toward an edge/rim.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__rpent__back_project(args: {
  // Camera to back-project from (default agentview).
  camera?: "agentview" | "wrist";
  // Pixel column (0=left) in the selected resolution image.
  col?: number | null;
  // Region mode: [c0, c1] pixel col window. Requires row_range.
  col_range?: Array<number> | null;
  // Coordinate system for row/col (default high). Use low only when row/col came from the embedded/standard 256 image.
  resolution?: "high" | "low";
  // Pixel row (0=top) in the selected resolution image.
  row?: number | null;
  // Region mode: [r0, r1] pixel row window. Requires col_range.
  row_range?: Array<number> | null;
  // Depth/world-map step; 0 = initial, -1 = latest.
  step?: number;
  // Region mode: keep only pixels with world z <= z_max.
  z_max?: number | null;
  // Region mode: keep only pixels with world z >= z_min.
  z_min?: number | null;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Servo position AND orientation (pitch + yaw) SIMULTANEOUSLY. Unlike move_to (holds orientation) + rotate_pitch (holds xyz), this co-varies xyz and wrist tilt every env.step. Use to thread cabinet-front / low-shelf poses where a decoupled position servo drives the wrist into an IK singularity and stalls.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__rpent__move_pose(args: {
  // OSC action scale (default 0.05)
  action_scale?: number;
  // Gripper command held during the move (default -1)
  gripper?: number;
  // Step budget (default 150)
  max_steps?: number;
  // Orientation tolerance, rad (default 0.05)
  ori_tol?: number;
  // Per-step pitch clip, rad (default 0.08)
  pitch_step?: number;
  // Per-step Δxyz cap, m (default 0.02)
  step_clip?: number;
  // Absolute pitch target, rad
  target_pitch?: number | null;
  // Absolute yaw target, rad
  target_yaw?: number | null;
  // Position tolerance, m (default 0.012)
  tol?: number;
  // World-frame target [x, y, z] in meters
  xyz: Array<number>;
  // Per-step yaw clip, rad (default 0.08)
  yaw_step?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Scripted EEF servo to a world-frame XYZ target via the OSC controller. Holds orientation (use rotate_wrist / rotate_pitch / move_pose to reorient). gripper: -1 = open, +1 = close. NEVER command a single move_to with |Δxy| > 0.30 — OSC flips IK and the run corrupts; split long traversal into 2-3 mid waypoints at carry z.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__rpent__move_to(args: {
  // OSC action scale (default 0.05)
  action_scale?: number;
  // Gripper command: -1 open, +1 close (default -1)
  gripper?: number;
  // Step budget (default 80)
  max_steps?: number;
  // Per-step Δxyz cap before action_scale, m (default 0.025)
  step_clip?: number;
  // Optional world-frame yaw target in radians
  target_yaw?: number | null;
  // Position tolerance, m (default 0.012)
  tol?: number;
  // World-frame target [x, y, z] in meters
  xyz: Array<number>;
  // Per-step yaw clip, rad (default 0.10)
  yaw_step_clip?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Pi0.5 closed-loop contact skill for non-pick interactions (e.g. stove/knob/button/short push). Returned success/task_success only mirrors official termination; for intermediate contact skills, success=false does not necessarily mean the contact interaction failed. Inspect image/state evidence. Do not use it as a general pick/place shortcut.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__rpent__pi0_doubled(args: {
  // Action-chunk budget (default 20)
  max_chunks?: number;
  // Contact-skill prompt, e.g. 'turn on the stove'.
  prompt: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Pi0.5 closed-loop pick. Use it for the grasp; YOU then do every move_to and release. Use modest max_chunks and verify the grasp from EEF lift, gripper closure, and available images.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__rpent__pi0_pick(args: {
  // Required descent before lift detection, m (default 0.10)
  descent_thresh?: number;
  // Finger-separation closed threshold (default 0.06)
  gripper_closed_thresh?: number;
  // Minimum finger separation accepted as a held object (default 0.0)
  gripper_open_thresh?: number;
  // EEF post-descent ascent threshold for success, m (default 0.05)
  lift_thresh?: number;
  // Action-chunk budget (default 24)
  max_chunks?: number;
  // Pi0 prompt (e.g. 'pick up the akita black bowl').
  prompt: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Open the gripper for up to max_steps env steps while holding EEF in place. Triggers libero termination if the matching On/In predicate is met.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__rpent__release(args: {
  // Step budget (default 20)
